Bound aggregate SVG offscreen and filter image memory.

Telegram-originated hardening, not an upstream backport. Each image QtSvg
allocates for a filter, mask, pattern or offscreen buffer is limited only by
the per-image allocation limit, but an untrusted document could keep one
filter region image alive per distinct result name and one buffer per nested
filtered element, many gigabytes in total.

For untrusted documents reserve every such image, and the transient workspace
of each filter primitive, from one budget owned by the document before it is
allocated, and return it when the last copy of the image is destroyed. Live
storage of these images stays at most B = clamp(24 * 4 * W * H bytes, 96 MiB,
768 MiB), where W x H is the largest root paint device the document was drawn
on. A denied allocation takes the existing "too big, ignoring" fallback, and
AssumeTrustedSource documents stay exempt as from the nesting limit.

